  "question": "<p>Let $\\Omega = \\{x \\in \\mathbb{R}^2 : x_1 \\ge 0, x_2 \\ge 0, x_1 + x_2 \\le 1\\}$. At $x^* = (0, 0)^\\top$, derive the cone of feasible directions $\\mathcal{F}(x^*)$ and the normal cone $N_\\Omega(x^*)$.</p>",
  "solution": "<p><b>Calculation:</b><br>1. <b>Active Constraints at $(0, 0)$:</b><br>$g_1(x) = -x_1 \\le 0$ (Active: $g_1(0,0) = 0$).<br>$g_2(x) = -x_2 \\le 0$ (Active: $g_2(0,0) = 0$).<br>$g_3(x) = x_1 + x_2 - 1 \\le 0$ (Inactive: $g_3(0,0) = -1 \\lt  0$). Active set $\\mathcal{A}(x^*) = \\{1, 2\\}$.</p><p>2. <b>Cone of Feasible Directions:</b><br>Since constraints are linear, $\\mathcal{F}(x^*) = T_{\\text{lin}}(x^*)$: $$\\nabla g_1(0, 0)^\\top d \\le 0 \\implies -d_1 \\le 0 \\implies d_1 \\ge 0.$$ $$\\nabla g_2(0, 0)^\\top d \\le 0 \\implies -d_2 \\le 0 \\implies d_2 \\ge 0.$$ Thus: $$\\mathcal{F}(x^*) = \\{ (d_1, d_2)^\\top \\in \\mathbb{R}^2 : d_1 \\ge 0, d_2 \\ge 0 \\} = \\mathbb{R}_+^2 \\quad (\\text{first quadrant}).$$</p><p>3. <b>Normal Cone $N_\\Omega(x^*)$:</b><br>The normal cone is the polar cone of the tangent cone: $$N_\\Omega(x^*) = \\{ v \\in \\mathbb{R}^2 : v^\\top d \\le 0 \\text{ for all } d \\in \\mathcal{F}(x^*) \\}.$$ For $v = (v_1, v_2)^\\top$, $v_1 d_1 + v_2 d_2 \\le 0$ for all $d_1 \\ge 0, d_2 \\ge 0$ requires $v_1 \\le 0$ and $v_2 \\le 0$. Thus: $$N_\\Omega(x^*) = \\{ (v_1, v_2)^\\top \\in \\mathbb{R}^2 : v_1 \\le 0, v_2 \\le 0 \\} = -\\mathbb{R}_+^2 \\quad (\\text{third quadrant}).$$</p>",
