  "question": "<p>Solve the problem using KKT conditions: $$\\min_{x_1, x_2} f(x) = (x_1 - 1)^2 + (x_2 - 2)^2 \\quad \\text{subject to} \\quad x_1 + x_2 \\le 1, \\quad x_1 \\ge 0, \\quad x_2 \\ge 0.$$</p>",
  "solution": "<p><b>Calculation:</b><br>1. <b>Standard Form:</b><br>$\\min f(x) = (x_1 - 1)^2 + (x_2 - 2)^2$ subject to: $g_1(x) = x_1 + x_2 - 1 \\le 0$, $g_2(x) = -x_1 \\le 0$, $g_3(x) = -x_2 \\le 0$.</p><p>2. <b>KKT Conditions:</b><br>Stationarity: $$\\begin{bmatrix} 2(x_1 - 1) \\\\ 2(x_2 - 2) \\end{bmatrix} + \\mu_1 \\begin{bmatrix} 1 \\\\ 1 \\end{bmatrix} + \\mu_2 \\begin{bmatrix} -1 \\\\ 0 \\end{bmatrix} + \\mu_3 \\begin{bmatrix} 0 \\\\ -1 \\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix} 0 \\\\ 0 \\end{bmatrix}.$$ Complementary slackness: $\\mu_1 (x_1 + x_2 - 1) = 0$, $\\mu_2 x_1 = 0$, $\\mu_3 x_2 = 0$. Dual feasibility: $\\mu_1, \\mu_2, \\mu_3 \\ge 0$.</p><p>3. <b>Case Analysis:</b></p><p>• <b>Unconstrained minimizer:</b> $(1, 2)$ has $x_1 + x_2 = 3 > 1$ (infeasible). So at least one constraint is active. <br>• <b>Test Case: $g_1$ active, $g_2, g_3$ inactive ($\\mu_2 = \\mu_3 = 0, \\mu_1 > 0$):</b><br>$x_1 + x_2 = 1 \\implies x_2 = 1 - x_1$. From stationarity: $2(x_1 - 1) + \\mu_1 = 0 \\implies \\mu_1 = 2(1 - x_1)$. $2(x_2 - 2) + \\mu_1 = 0 \\implies \\mu_1 = 2(2 - x_2) = 2(2 - (1 - x_1)) = 2(1 + x_1)$. Equate expressions for $\\mu_1$: $$2(1 - x_1) = 2(1 + x_1) \\implies 1 - x_1 = 1 + x_1 \\implies 2x_1 = 0 \\implies x_1 = 0.$$ Then $x_2 = 1 - 0 = 1$. Multiplier: $\\mu_1 = 2(1 - 0) = 2 > 0$. Now check $x_1 = 0$: $g_2(x) = -x_1 = 0$, so $g_2$ is ALSO active! <br>• <b>Case: $g_1$ and $g_2$ active ($x_1 = 0, x_1 + x_2 = 1 \\implies x_2 = 1$):</b><br>$g_3$ is inactive ($x_2 = 1 > 0 \\implies \\mu_3 = 0$). Stationarity: $$2(0 - 1) + \\mu_1 - \\mu_2 = 0 \\implies -2 + \\mu_1 - \\mu_2 = 0,$$ $$2(1 - 2) + \\mu_1 = 0 \\implies -2 + \\mu_1 = 0 \\implies \\mu_1 = 2.$$ Substitute $\\mu_1 = 2$ into first equation: $$-2 + 2 - \\mu_2 = 0 \\implies \\mu_2 = 0.$$ Check dual feasibility: $\\mu_1 = 2 \\ge 0$, $\\mu_2 = 0 \\ge 0$, $\\mu_3 = 0 \\ge 0$. Check primal feasibility: $x_1 = 0 \\ge 0$, $x_2 = 1 \\ge 0$, $x_1 + x_2 = 1 \\le 1$. All KKT conditions are satisfied! Since the objective is strictly convex and constraints are convex, $x^* = (0, 1)^\\top$ is the unique global minimizer. Minimum value: $f(0, 1) = (0 - 1)^2 + (1 - 2)^2 = 1 + 1 = 2$.</p>",
