  "question": "<p>Solve the water-filling problem: $\\min_{x} -\\sum_{i=1}^n \\log(\\alpha_i + x_i)$ subject to $\\sum_{i=1}^n x_i = 1, x_i \\ge 0$, where $\\alpha_i > 0$.</p>",
  "solution": "<p><b>Calculation:</b><br>1. <b>Lagrangian:</b><br>$$\\mathcal{L}(x, \\nu, \\lambda) = -\\sum_{i=1}^n \\log(\\alpha_i + x_i) + \\nu \\left(\\sum_{i=1}^n x_i - 1\\right) - \\sum_{i=1}^n \\lambda_i x_i.$$</p><p>2. <b>KKT Conditions:</b></p><p>• Stationarity: $-\\frac{1}{\\alpha_i + x_i} + \\nu - \\lambda_i = 0 \\implies \\nu - \\lambda_i = \\frac{1}{\\alpha_i + x_i}$. <br>• Complementary slackness: $\\lambda_i x_i = 0$ with $\\lambda_i \\ge 0, x_i \\ge 0$.</p><p>3. <b>Derive Water-filling Solution:</b></p><p>• If $x_i > 0$, then $\\lambda_i = 0$, so $\\nu = \\frac{1}{\\alpha_i + x_i} \\implies \\alpha_i + x_i = \\frac{1}{\\nu} \\implies x_i = \\frac{1}{\\nu} - \\alpha_i$. <br>• If $x_i = 0$, then $\\lambda_i \\ge 0$, so $\\nu = \\frac{1}{\\alpha_i} + \\lambda_i \\ge \\frac{1}{\\alpha_i} \\implies \\frac{1}{\\nu} \\le \\alpha_i$. Combining both cases into a single expression: $$x_i^* = \\max\\left(0, \\, \\frac{1}{\\nu} - \\alpha_i\\right) = \\left( \\frac{1}{\\nu} - \\alpha_i \\right)_+.$$ The parameter $1/\\nu$ represents the \"water level\". Substitute into the primal equality constraint: $$\\sum_{i=1}^n \\max\\left(0, \\, \\frac{1}{\\nu} - \\alpha_i\\right) = 1.$$ The function $g(1/\\nu) = \\sum_{i=1}^n (1/\\nu - \\alpha_i)_+$ is piecewise linear, continuous, and strictly increasing. The water level $1/\\nu$ is uniquely determined by bisection or sorting $\\alpha_i$.</p>",
